      "question": "What are the key elements of the differential diagnosis, and how does this case distinguish SAH from other causes of acute headache?",
      "my_answer": "Differentials include migraine, meningitis, intracerebral hemorrhage, and reversible cerebral vasoconstriction syndrome (RCVS). This case favors SAH due to thunderclap onset, loss of consciousness, CT-confirmed subarachnoid blood, and an identified aneurysm.",
