      "rationale": "Nimodipine reduces vasospasm risk. BP should be controlled (typically SBP <160 mmHg) to reduce re-bleed risk without compromising perfusion. The patient needs neurointensive care monitoring for hydrocephalus, vasospasm, and delayed cerebral ischemia."
